# Everything, then re-admit what the build needs.
#
# An allow-list rather than a deny-list, because the failure modes point opposite
# ways: a forgotten deny entry ships something into an image — bin/, a local
# appsettings, a .git directory with credentials in its history — and a forgotten
# allow entry only fails the build.
**

!src/
!tools/
!Directory.Build.props
!Directory.Packages.props
!global.json
!NuGet.config

# .editorconfig is part of the build, not an editor preference.
#
# Analyzer severities live in it, including the suppressions that make this
# codebase compile under TreatWarningsAsErrors. Leaving it out meant the image
# built with different rules than the developer machine and failed on
# suppressions that exist — a "works on my machine" of the most confusing kind,
# because the code was identical and only the invisible configuration differed.
!.editorconfig

# Build output from the host. Copying it in makes the image depend on whatever
# was last built locally, which is how a container works on one machine and not
# another.
**/bin/
**/obj/

# Local configuration and anything holding a secret.
**/appsettings.*.Local.json
**/*.user
**/.env
